 "source_url": "https://www.instagram.com/reel/DbfQBXtBK5N/",
 "title": "4 Effective Networking Questions to Build High-Value Connections",
 "topic": "communication",
 "summary": "The creator shares four strategic questions to ask at networking events to build valuable relationships. These questions help create memorable interactions and provide smooth excuses to follow up later.",
 "key_points": [
  "Ask for their favorite book or podcast recommendation to establish a reason to follow up with them later.",
  "Ask about the most exciting project they worked on this year to evoke positive emotions, as people remember how you made them feel.",
  "Inquire about the biggest problem they are trying to solve this quarter so you can reach out later with relevant articles, tools, or contacts.",
  "When presenting a business or service, ask if they know anyone else who might benefit, making it a lower-effort request."
 ],
 "content": "Post text: #networking hacks 101  Make a note of this post.  Transcript: 10 out of 10 questions to ask at a networking event to make rich connections that get increasingly more valuable. Ask for their favorite book or podcast recommendation, that way you have an excuse to follow up on them later. Ask them what's the most exciting project they worked on this year, because people don't remember what you say, they remember what you made them feel. Ask what's the biggest problem they're trying to solve this quarter, that way you have an excuse to follow up if you see an article, a tool, or a relevant contact you can introduce them with, you can follow up with them. If you have a business or a service, instead of asking directly if they're interested, ask them if they know anyone that would be interested and would benefit, that way it's a way lower effort ask.  On-screen text: - 10/10 Rich People Networking Q's - 10/10 Rich Networking Q's: - Q.1 - Q.2 - Q.3 - Q.4",
